# Comments and formatting

Comment source as you write it: files, types, functions, and non-obvious branches.

- Conversational and straightforward. Explain why, not a restatement of the next line.
- Non verbose. No comment-every-line.
- No long dashes (no em dash or en dash). Use a comma, period, or hyphen.
- Format with Prettier (`npm run format`). Do not hand-format.

```ts
// Bad: restates the code, uses a long dash, and is noisy.
// Load the CSV — this reads the file from disk
const raw = await readFile(csvPath, 'utf8')

// Good: says why the branch exists.
// Basketball-Reference dumps a league-average row. Drop it so ranks stay player-only.
if (playerId === LEAGUE_AVERAGE_ID) continue
```
